rica’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/77903"} "Madeline Manning"] ", who had won the 1967 AAU in 2:03.6. But the favorite’s in the final probably fell to Dutchwoman " [:a {:href "/athletes/73731"} "Mia Gommers"] ". In the final Manning went to the lead at the bell and nobody could pass her, as she won by almost 15 metres in an Olympic record 2:00.9. Romania’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/75150"} "Ileana Silai"] " edged Gommers for the silver."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "97"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/77903"} "Madeline Manning"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "2:08.7 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "2:05.8 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "2:00.9 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "215"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/75150"} "Ileana Silai"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ROU"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ROU.png"}] "ROU"]] [:td {} "2:04.1 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "2:05.9 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "2:02.5 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "148"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/73731"} "Mia Gommers"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]] [:td {} "2:04.0 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "2:05.1 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "2:02.6 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:t